      "widgets_values": [
        "A documentary close-up of the real single crystal silicon boule in this photograph. The industrial ingot has a heavy reflective cylindrical body, fine concentric growth striations, a tapered shoulder and a thin seed neck. The camera makes a slow lateral dolly and a slight rise from the cylinder toward its tapered shoulder, creating natural parallax and changing reflections on the fixed solid surface. Preserve the exact shape and position of the silicon boule. Crisp silver metallic ridges, realistic workshop photography, neutral light, authentic manufacturing detail. One controlled continuous camera move. No growth transformation, no bending, no lettering, no overlays."
      ]
